Back of the envelope estimation
Total registered users~300million ,
daily active users -> 50 million, out of each person , assume 100 requests per second (includes browsing , search, add to cart), 
so, total requests per day = 50 million * 100 = 5 billion requests / day. , which is 5 billion / (86400) = 58K RPS . Peak RPS = 10 * 58K = 580K RPS.
E-commerce is ready heavy system , order estimation = 5% of daily active users = 2.5 million buyers /day , so approximately , 2.5 million orders / day ,
peak sale = 10x = 25 million buyers / day.
So, storage estimation :- 2.5 M * 1 KB = 2.5 GB / day
so, storage per  year = 2.5GB * 365  = 1 TB / year

data size hierarchy :-
Unit	Full Form	Approx Size
bit (b)	Binary digit	0 or 1
Byte (B)	8 bits	1 character
KB	Kilobyte	~1,000 Bytes
MB	Megabyte	~1,000 KB
GB	Gigabyte	~1,000 MB
TB	Terabyte	~1,000 GB
PB	Petabyte	~1,000 TB

Database choice :- 
now, for maintaing the user profile , user database (sql) is required which stores user name , first name , last name , email.
, we can also have database for storing the address , because a user can have mutliple addresses.
for product table , nosql database like mongodb or dynamodb can be used.
for reviews , key-value db can be stored.

Core APIs to be used :-
1) using get api to get the product catalog
2) addToCart(userId,productId,qty,amount) -> returns true or false , that whether product is added or not.
3) Place order (userId,productId,addressId,paymentStatus) -> return true or false , that whether order is placed or not.
4) Check order status using get api , and it will return the status of the order


High Level Architecture :- Implementations of core apis.






